tStreamEvent`; with `skill_id` for a sub-agent), names a leaf tool call when the model starts it (native `ToolUseStreamEvent`), and `skill_tool` carries `input` and, on the result, `tool_name` + `output` (cut at `RON_DEEP_RESEARCH_TOOL_OUTPUT_CHARS`, 8000) + `output_truncated`; a framework plugin tool's result is not a tool row. The run keeps each agent's transcript (`nodes[..].activity`: text, reasoning, skill, pass) and each sub-agent's (`skill_invocations[].steps`: text, reasoning, tool), folded identically server-side (`_apply_event_locked`) and in `reduceDeepResearchEvent`, so a finished run reopens as it looked live; the per-node skill copies and `GET /deep-research/runs` leave transcripts and tool payloads out (`_without_transcripts`), `normalizeDeepResearchSnapshot` keeps what a fuller snapshot gave, and `refreshRuns` does not merge a listing into a run whose stream is attached. Runs saved before transcripts render from their skills and previews. Tests: `test_deep_research_graph.py::test_run_transcripts_keep_reasoning_and_tool_payloads_and_lists_leave_them_out`, `src/lib/deep-research-api.test.ts`, `src/lib/deep-research-graph.test.ts`. **The formation is set by `FORMATION_TOPOLOGY`** (`build_deep_research_graph` builds Strands from it; the renderer's `DEFAULT_FORMATION_TOPOLOGY` mirrors it): outer `Graph` `research_swarm` (Swarm: a researcher fanning out parallel `subagent`s, a reference fact checker, a citation manager, QA) → `data_analysis_graph` (Graph: visual planner → data analyst → visual citation → QA) → `writing_swarm` (Swarm: report and deck designers, layout QA, report writer + QA, deck writer + QA) → `production_graph` (Graph: `pdf_publisher`⇄`pdf_qa` and `deck_producer`⇄`deck_build_qa` in parallel). A Graph QA ends its reply with `APPROVED` or `REVISE: <agent>`; `qa_requests_revision` (the Strands feedback-loop edge condition) sends the work back to that agent and the chain returns to QA, at most `max_refinements` times (`RON_DEEP_RESEARCH_MAX_R