dk`). **Streamed tool calls are correlated by `ToolCall.index`, not `id`** (`_ToolCallAssembler`): on the documented wire only the first fragment of a call carries `id`/`name`; argument fragments repeat `index` and omit `id`, which the installed SDK defaults to the literal `"null"`. The vended loop (and Ron's copy of it until 2026-10-21) grouped by `id`, so GLM 5.3 produced one named call with `{}` arguments plus a phantom `"null"` call holding the real arguments — the native loop then dispatched the named call and the tool failed `Validation failed for input parameters` (`tool_catalog`, `shell`, …). The assembler keeps the validated identity, concatenates string fragments, serializes documented object-valued arguments, and raises `MistralStreamError` instead of dispatching for: two ids/names on one index, a continuation with no identity, incomplete/invalid argument JSON, `finish_reason: error`, or an EOF while a call is buffered; `length` keeps native `max_tokens` semantics (no dispatch). `tool_choice` (`auto|any|tool`) is translated onto the documented field (unsupported shapes raise); HTTP errors are classified by `MistralError.status_code` (429/503 → `ModelThrottledException`), not by message text; `stream=False` and `structured_output` go through the same client (so `max` applies) and the same assembler. Tests: `test_mistral_tool_stream.py` (real `mistralai` SSE parsing over `httpx.MockTransport` → `RonMistralModel` → native `Agent` → a required-parameter recording tool). **Gemini** `GEMINI_THINKING_LEVELS_BY_MODEL` — the "Controlling thinking" table at ai.google.dev/gemini-api/docs/thinking plus the image-generation guide, confirmed live on `generateContent` with `include_thoughts=True`: 3.8/3.7 Flash and `gemini-flash-latest` `low|medium|high` (MINIMAL rejected), 3.6/3.5 Flash, 3.5 Flash-Lite, 3.1 Flash-Lite, 3 Flash Preview, `gemini-flash-lite-latest`, Robotics-ER 2 `minimal|low|medium|high`, 3.1 Pro (+`-customtools`, `gemini-pro-latest`), 2.5 Pro/Flash/Flash-Lite `low|medium|high`, 3 Pro Preview `low|high`, Nano Banana 2.1 `minimal|medium|high`, 3.1 Flash Image / Flash-Lite Image `minimal|high`; TTS, transcribe, omni, computer-use, 2.5 Flash Image and Nano Banana Pro return `[]` (`"Thinking level is not supported for this model"`). The effort is sent as `ThinkingConfig(include_thoughts=True, thinking_level=<UPPER>)`. The Live/`/bidi` picker is separate (`endpoints/bidi.py` `EFFORTS`, `src/lib/voice-settings.ts`). The renderer pickers (`AgentPanel`, `IssueRonChat`, `SuperAgentInterface`) use `ModelSelector`, which always shows the chosen model's levels (none for a model without any; "Auto" sends no effort), and send `reasoning_effort` on the first `/chat`. NIM's gateway accepts its whole generic enum for any model (live 2026-11-10), so NIM levels cannot be confirmed by probing and its reference page for `z-ai/glm-5.3-flash` documents no `reasoning_effort`; `low|high|max` there follows Mistral's documented and live-verified values for the same model. Tests: `test_chat.py` (`*_efforts_are_documented_not_probed`, `test_mistral_and_gemini_build_model_validate_effort`), `test_mistral_model.py`.
